<title>USA: Magnum Petroleum sets 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Magnum Petroleum sets 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magnum Petroleum Inc said Tuesday directors approved a budget of $15 million for fiscal 1997 to fund the capital costs.</p>
<p>Included in this budget is the development of five waterflood projects located in West Texas and the drilling of a minimum of 10 wells per quarter on the &quot;Panoma&quot; properties acquired at the end of June 1996 from Meridian Oil Inc, a subsidiary of Burlington Resources Inc.</p>
<p>About 20 percent of the 1997 capital budget will be directed at exploratory projects located primarily in Oklahoma and Texas. -- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
